# LIFE-867: started by lifeos-honcho-meter-alert.path when the meter writes EXHAUSTED. One Agent Inbox alert through the one alert command (LIFE-876, honcho-alerts client); the leading `-` makes a failed alert
# harmless. The EXHAUSTED file stays as the durable signal. No secret and no personal data in the subject or details.
[Unit]
Description=LIFE OS Honcho budget stopped: one Agent Inbox alert

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=root
ExecStart=-/opt/lifeos-buzz-mcp/current/bin/honcho-alert send "Honcho budget stopped (EXHAUSTED)" "The Honcho metering proxy refused a request because this month's cap is spent or the budget cannot be verified. Reason, window and time are in /var/lib/lifeos-honcho-meter/EXHAUSTED. Inference is stopped until the next window starts (the 5th at 6:00 PM CT); memory is untouched. A raise of the cap needs Jim's approval." --urgency Today
